  "result": "longer_training_with_a_gentle_lr_restart_reaches_near_teacher_tracking",
  "conclusion": "Continuing from step499 to step999 with a gentle learning-rate restart raises final held-out tracking from 52.5% to 94.2%, mean stage accuracy from 65.6% to 97.5%, and lowers memory cosine loss from 0.396 to 0.122. The three stage accuracies are 100.0%, 98.3%, and 94.2%. This rejects memory capacity and an inherently unlearnable direct-visual interface as the primary explanation for the earlier failure. The apparent step450-499 plateau was predominantly under-optimization caused by the low learning-rate tail. Remaining errors concentrate after the third recurrent update; before changing capacity or inference structure, confirm variance with fixed validation episodes and multiple seeds, then target third-update hard examples or a short low-rate continuation."
